Backport of Home Assistant's PKCE S256 support (RFC 7636), taken from home-assistant/core.

Home Assistant's OAuth server advertises and implements PKCE S256 only from 2026.10.0 on. ChatGPT
refuses to create the connector against an instance whose /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
omits "code_challenge_methods_supported": ["S256"], so the release nixpkgs pins today (2026.9.4)
cannot be connected at all. This patch carries the upstream fix on that release.

Upstream commit, re-anchored onto this release (same changes, context lines from the installed
sources; tests omitted):
  7398141b4c  Support PKCE S256 in OAuth server (#181957)

Adaptation: the upstream hunk was cut after the voluptuous alias had been renamed to "probatio"; this
tree still imports "voluptuous as vol", so the references read "vol."

Delete this file and the "patches" override in nixos.nix as soon as nixpkgs ships Home Assistant
2026.10.x, and verify the result with:
  curl -s https://hass.vyrx.de/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server | grep code_challenge

